[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Narrow scalar storage and checked conversion continuation

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: CIL-STORAGE-001
TITLE: Declared scalar storage and interface widths
STATEMENT: >>>
The scheduled frontend shall accept byte, sbyte, short, ushort and char locals,
arguments and results. Writes truncate to declared storage width; loads extend
to the 32-bit evaluation stack according to declared signedness. Ports use the
declared scalar width. Capture inputs only on accepted start, clear locals and
results on start/reset, preserve original IL provenance and reject unsupported
wide, native and floating storage. Preserve the existing canonical Boolean profile.
Verification: ScheduledScalarStorageTests and independent native HDL replay.
<<<
